SUMMARY:How to Engage Un-engaged Voters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T170000
UID:d54dc9aefbedc890f056a6b9842a8ed8@mobilize.us
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://mobilize-uploads-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/u
 ploads/event/How%20to%20Engage%20Voters%20-%20Mobilize_2026052719134820192
 0.png
DESCRIPTION:Please join Precinct 44.1 and welcome Heather Heckel\, PhD\, a
  long-time teacher and practitioner of advocacy and community engagement t
 o discuss: * How we can effectively connect with people with whom we somet
 imes disagree. * How we can engage those who are not yet motivated to vote
 . * What well-meaning strategies might "backfire." * How we can reduce pol
 arization. * How we can use our time most effectively to amplify our voice
 s\, magnify our impact and strengthen our community. Light refreshments
LOCATION:Enka-Candler Library\, 1404 Sand Hill Rd\, Candler\, NC\, 28715
URL:https://www.mobilize.us/buncombedems/event/961472/
