X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Ashevillehikinggroup": "https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315743309/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ashevillehikinggroup
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_315743309@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260721T032835Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T123000
SUMMARY:MTS Trail South Out-and-Back\, 6 mi. 650ft. Elev. Gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nWe'll meet at the parking lot in f
 ront of **Haywood Appliance** and **Fresh Market** on Hendersonville Road.
  From there\, we hop onto the Mountains-to-Sea Trail and head south for a 
 simple out-and-back\, a relatively mild 3 miles each way.\n\nWe'll take a 
 15-minute break at the turnaround point.\n\nDogs are welcome\, but they mu
 st be leashed in accordance with Forest Service regulations.\n\n**MEETING 
 TIME & DIRECTIONS**\n\nWe'll gather at 9:00 AM on the south side of the Fr
 esh Market parking lot in front of the Haywood Appliance store. The addres
 s is 1378 Hendersonville Rd. Look for me at my silver Hyundai.\n\nLink for
  Google Maps: [Fresh Market Parking Lot](https://maps.app.goo.gl/VBNrrBeuU
 SnLeU3j6)\n\nWe'll try to set out by **9:05**.\n\n**COURTESY TO WAIT-LISTE
 RS (Please!)**\n\nOnly sign up if you \\*truly\\* plan to come. If you mus
 t cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as soon as possible so
  wait-listers will have sufficient notice. (The same goes if you're on the
  waitlist and know you can't attend. Please switch to "Not Going.") And pl
 ease please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n\n**WEATHER**\n\nWe'll watch the w
 eather and post a cancellation message by 7:30 AM if the forecast is >50% 
 chance of precipitation.\n\n**GUESTS**\n\nIf you'd like to bring a guest\,
  please have them join the Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for the hike
  on their own. In\n\n**LEGALESE**\n\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event inv
 olves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. 
 Participants are responsible for their own safety and affirm that they hav
 e the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplie
 s. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike org
 anizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all
  risks. Participants assume full responsibility for any injuries\, damages
 \, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315743309
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260719T021420Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260719T021420Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
