X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Jackofthewood Events Ics": "https://jackofthewood.com/events/jess-jill-full-band-show/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:jackofthewood_events_ics
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:12006@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260801T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260801T233000
DTSTAMP:20260605T233119Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/jess-jill-full-band-show/
SUMMARY:Jess &amp\; Jill (Full Band Show)
DESCRIPTION:\nJesse and Jillian\, aka “Jess and Jill” met on a dusty st
 age in Key West\, Florida. Right away\, there was an undeniable force of c
 hemistry between them. Soon after meeting\, they formed their musical duo\
 , and have been playing music together nearly every day since. They have b
 een awarded “Duo of the Year” in Key West for the past three years.&nb
 sp\;\n\n\n\nTheir musical style fits under the umbrella “Americana” wi
 th influences ranging from Jerry Garcia to Joni Mitchell to Gillian Welch 
 and David Rawlings. They are working on an album of original music at Echo
  Mountain Recording in Asheville\, NC. Their original music dances gleeful
 ly across the borders of genre\, with one song described as “reminiscent
  of Pink Floyd\, The Grateful Dead\, and a sense of vulnerability.” Othe
 r tunes drive with zest of bluegrass\, dance with a Celtic\, worldly feel\
 , and groove with a swampy\, funk flavor. The thing that binds it all toge
 ther? Their approach to the music as one musician - present\, honest\, and
  vulnerable.\n\n\n\nJesse Wagner was born in between Philadelphia and Alle
 ntown. He was raised in Telford\, Pennsylvania. Jesse studied privately wi
 th Dennis Sandole\, Ben Schachter\, and Craig Ebener. He founded “The Ha
 ppy Dog\,” a band known best for their covers of The Grateful Dead\, whi
 ch brought him to Key West in 2011. Jesse stopped leaving Key West a few y
 ears later.&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nJillian Todd is from Potsdam\, NY. Her musical b
 ackground is rooted in theater and dance. Months after graduating from col
 lege in 2021\, Jillian moved to Key West to work as an actor at the histor
 ic Waterfront Playhouse. Soon after moving\, she was compelled to work as 
 a musician\, and devoted herself to the guitar and songwriting. \n\n\n\nM
 usic 8:30-11:30pm $10 cover at the door.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://www.yout
 ube.com/watch?v=2ShCBevZWIM&amp\;t=61s\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/
 watch?v=oJdxAPOIrBo&amp\;t=37s\n\n\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/04/jessandjill1-scaled.webp
END:VEVENT
