DTSTAMP:20260718T213047Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/old-time-jam-4-2026-08-26/
SUMMARY:OLD-TIME JAM
DESCRIPTION:\nThe roots of Appalachian old-time music stretch far across th
 e Atlantic and we're proud to honor and showcase that legacy at Jack of th
 e Wood Pub with our long-running Old-Time Jam sessions — every Wednesda
 y starting at 5pm! Recently recommended by Rolling Stone for "those lookin
 g for an organic\, participatory [music] experience" in Asheville\, the Ol
 d-Time Jam is one of several weekly traditional jam sessions hosted at JAC
 K.\n\n\n\nOur cozy Celtic pub is the perfect spot downtown to take in some
  of the region's finest traditional acoustic musicians playing "in the rou
 nd" while you enjoy a pint or two and the best pub fare in town!\n\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 5/09/JOTW_WED-OldTimeJam_2025-RollingStoneQuote_IG_1080x1350.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Writers": "https://www.meetup.com/avl-writers/events/phwgztyjclbjc/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_writers
X-SOURCE:AVL Writers
UID:event_phwgztyjclbjc@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260721T032843Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260826T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260826T200000
SUMMARY:Weekly Critique
DESCRIPTION:AVL Writers\nThis is the standing weekly critique. Bring anyth
 ing new you're working on to share with the group. If you don't have a pro
 ject to share\, you are most welcome to attend\, discuss\, and get inspire
 d.\n\nFor our group discussion\, please bring at least 8-10 printed copies
  of your piece. That way\, we can all read through each other's work and p
 rovide feedback.\n\nSharing our creative efforts is an important part of t
 he writing process. I'm really looking forward to reading what you've been
  working on. Don't worry if it's still a rough draft.\n\nIf you're having 
 trouble finding us\, look for a placard on the table with the group's name
 .\n\nIf you would like to join our group email list for updates regarding 
 contests\, events\, and more [you can sign up on our website](https://avlw
 riters.com/).
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-writers/events/phwgztyjclbjc/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260709T180135Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260709T180135Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
